# scan-download — GuardDog allowlist
#
# One substring per line. Any GuardDog indicator whose match block contains a
# line listed here is treated as known-benign and subtracted from the count.
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# SAFETY: entries are GLOBAL (apply to every repo you scan). Keep them specific.
# A broad entry like "telegram" could hide a real exfiltration indicator in some
# other package. Prefer exact, narrow strings. Everything stays in the full log
# regardless — the allowlist only changes the pass/fail verdict.
#
# Examples (uncomment / adapt as you vet findings):
#
# api.telegram.org          # legit Telegram bot notification endpoint
# TOOL_ICON_MAP[prefix      # benign TypeScript dynamic dispatch (icon lookup)
